{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls","id":913999,"title":"Hunters and Ghouls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-14T04:29:59-07:00","id":913999,"title":"Hunters and Ghouls?","content":"How would the different compacts and conspiracies react to one of their members being / becoming a ghoul? Would you kill him or her? Would they use his new found powers against the supernaturals till he became mortal again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10398-dsoms","name":"DSOMS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:36:35-07:00","id":914001,"title":"","content":"IIRC the head of the Malleus Maleficarum is one, and pretty ancient at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:38:15-07:00","id":914002,"title":"","content":"It depends. If I was running it, there'd probably be a heavy leaning towards distrust and killing them, since they're likely an addict to vampire Vitae and probably the direct servant of a vampire. But the ghoul would, of course, have a chance to hide it since it isn't necessarily obvious to observation.<br /> <br /> My characters would likely kill them, but my hunter had a thing against vampires and my werewolf likes eating people.<br /> <br /> The idea of them using their powers against other supernaturals fits, it's what the leader of the Malleus Maleficarum does. But giving up limited immortality and supernatural powers isn't really an easy thing to do, especially given the addictive nature of Vitae. Plus you're likely to be more susceptible to certain vampire abilities, depending on where you're getting the Vitae from.<br /> <br /> In short, it's doable, but given the how the Vinculum works, shouldn't be doable for long without very rare and special circumstances. The head of the Malleus Maleficarum, for instance, seems to be a rogue ghoul whose entire conspiracy works, unknowingly, to capture vampires for him to drink. Presumably he keeps them staked and 'on tap.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:46:53-07:00","id":914009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914001#post914001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the head of the Malleus Maleficarum is one, and pretty ancient at that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, i knew that, but do the members of the Malleus Maleficarum know this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10398-dsoms","name":"DSOMS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:50:03-07:00","id":914011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914002#post914002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My characters would likely kill them, but my hunter had a thing against vampires and my werewolf likes eating people.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine would properbly too, but i had this idea of hunters capturing a vampire and then chaining them and constantly draining them for their blood so that it always was i torpor and then feeding it blood from blood banks when you need a refreshing dosis of vamp-blood. Would hunter organizations not kill people like them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10398-dsoms","name":"DSOMS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:52:13-07:00","id":914013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSOMS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914009#post914009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, i knew that, but do the members of the Malleus Maleficarum know this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of them don't, and aren't even aware he's still alive. Compacts and Conspiracies mentions that the current 'official' leader does know, and is disgusted by the whole thing and is plotting to destroy him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSOMS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914011#post914011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine would properbly too, but i had this idea of hunters capturing a vampire and then chaining them and constantly draining them for their blood so that it always was i torpor and then feeding it blood from blood banks when you need a refreshing dosis of vamp-blood. Would hunter organizations not kill people like them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to say it again but it depends. I'm not sure if a vampire in torpor can 'digest' blood and turn it to Vitae, that might be up to you. And a vampire has to spend Willpower to make you a ghoul, at least the first time you drink their Vitae, it's not something you can just get from drinking their blood while they're in torpor. Though Hunter: Night Stalkers offers some specialized rules for this.<br /> <br /> But most hunters would probably think less of a hunter cell that's a bunch of blood addicts, even if they were using their powers to kill supernaturals. But presumably they wouldn't advertise the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2016, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T05:07:54-07:00","id":914017,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Where there is a Cheiron, there is a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T05:08:09-07:00","id":914018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914013#post914013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But most hunters would probably think less of a hunter cell that's a bunch of blood addicts, even if they were using their powers to kill supernaturals. But presumably they wouldn't advertise the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank you, you have been very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10398-dsoms","name":"DSOMS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10398_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T05:09:12-07:00","id":914020,"title":"","content":"I assume that, in general, such members won't be accepted into the more organized hunter groups- 1st Tier cells may or may not accept such member, depending on the ideology of the specific members. Certain compacts, like the Long Night or the Night Watch, would reject such members from their organization, either out of ideology or because such people are controlled in many ways by another being, and so can't be trusted (although I could see a Long Night hunter getting into ghouldom and trying to go out as a &quot;test of faith&quot;). Some of those compacts would try to &quot;redeem&quot; the hunter (like the Talbot group) while others would simply try to kill him. Some compacts, however, may be more than willing to work with such hunters- an Ashwood Abbey member who start to see the effects of old age on her body would have little issues with using selling her soul to vampires, and it may even be an accepted behavior in certain Chapter Houses. The Promethean Brotherhood already use blasphemous ritual to steal the powers of witches, why doing so with vampires shouldn't be done? (of course, giving up some of your free will may be frowned upon, and there is a descent chance someone in the compact would try to preform the Rite on you- but other than that, all is good).<br /> <br /> Conspiracies are an whole other story. Those are a very suspicious organizations, after all, and loyalty to the conspiracy is the most important value. There is a reason why the MM's leader hide his presence, and why the vampire- VALKYRIE connection could trigger a civil war. The Lucifuge are already damn- who would be crazy enough to twice damn himself? Cheiron Group butcher and scavenge the bodies of monsters- are you sure you want to risk being harvested into organs? The members of the Cainte Heresy were all once victims of vampire abuse, some even being former ghouls. Going to search blood from vampires like and addict is a fate worse than death- and they would make sure you'll take the &quot;better path&quot;. Even groups without such issues with vampires, like the AKD or the AO, would suspect such members as vampire spies, while VASCU would probably just send you to one of their Suicide Squads. Maybe the Faithful of Shulpae, with their faith that eating monsters grants you divinity, could accept such behavior- but even they prefer to each the vampire as whole and not piece by piece, and who knows when one of them would flip and wonder if you are &quot;divine enough&quot; to eat.<br /> <br /> In sort, such thing could be done more easily in lower Tiers, and even then it could be problematic. The Vigil, after all, is made out of bonds of trust between hunters who stand back to back against the monsters. When one of the members is more like the monsters they hunt than they are, especially when such transformation force another being's will upon him, those bonds start to stretch and break. The more that trust is needed, the more fragile is that trust, and there are bigger chances of you getting killed by your former friends...<br /> <br /> But there are, of course, exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T05:26:03-07:00","id":914024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSOMS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913999-hunters-and-ghouls?p=914018#post914018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, thank you, you have been very helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope I wasn't too discouraging.<br /> <br /> All said and done, rules as written it's doable but difficult. The characters might have to hide it, deal with a vampire master who wants them to be hunters, have some sort of ability that makes them immune to the Vinculum, and so forth.<br /> <br /> But there's just as many rules that can support it, or you can toss out the rules and setting conceits altogether and do what you want, as it is a good hook. There's vampires whose blood doesn't inflict the Vinculum. They might be able to get Vitae from the garden of a vampire they've slain, whose plants make Vitae providing it's 'fed' vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:11:01-07:00","id":914046,"title":"","content":"If they know anything about Vampires they will probably assume that the Ghoul's will is not their own. I'm surprised that so many people would jump straight to killing. The Ghoul was a Cell member, and Hunters save each other's lives all the time. I think they would most likely stage an intervention or outright imprison the compromised member until the Vinculum lapses. You didn't mention how would that member become a Ghoul and it's an important detail. The Hunters would treat someone forced into Ghouldom differently than someone who sold out. Also, their reaction might be different if that member betrayed them at any point. At any rate, the Hunters might want to target the Vampire first, hoping (correctly) that killing them would shatter the bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 06-14-2016, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:23:59-07:00","id":914271,"title":"","content":"I say whatever makes for the better story! Do you feel the drama of the character trying to hide his new state, and possible addiction would be thrilling? Then go for it! It is more interesting to play out the debate of the Cell trying to determine if they should still trust their brother now that he is a thrall to a monster, or simply kill him? If so, rock on with it! Even if the group comes to the conclusion that being a ghoul makes you more powerful, therefore a better Hunter, and the whole Cell sets off to find Domintors to give them access to power, it could be really interesting. If the rules get in the way of a compelling story, feel free to fudge them. I also search for what serves the story and drama the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}